      "roles_v": 1,
      "summary": "STATE OF MAINE \nSUPREME JUDICIAL COURT \nSTANDING ORDER ON SERVICEMEMBERS OR SPOUSES OF SERVICEMEMBERS \nSEEKING ADMISSION TO THE MAINE BAR \n \nEffective August 3, 2026 \nAttorneys who are servicemembers or spouses of servicemembers \nassigned to Maine and who wish to be licensed in Maine while they or their \nspouses are stationed here may seek waiver of strict compliance with the \nduration of practice requirement of the rule g overning admission by motion \nwithout examination, Maine Bar Admission Rule 11A(a)(2).  The Maine \nSupreme Judicial Court, the Maine Board of Overseers of the Bar, and the Maine \nBoard of Bar Examiners are committed to working with these applicants to \naccommodate their unique circumstances and to expedite the bar application \nprocess to the extent possible when they or their spouses’ service brings them \nto Maine. \nThe Court will consider requests for waiver on a case -by-case basis, \ndepending on the individual circumstances of the applicant.   Servicemembers \nand spouses of servicemembers are encouraged to contact the Maine Supreme \nJudicial Court Clerk’s Office at (207)822-4146 for more information about the \nwaiver process. Servicemembers and spouses of servicemembers assigned to \nMaine who wish to take the Maine bar examination but have missed a deadline \nto apply for the exam, should also contact the Maine Board of Bar Examiners at \n(207)623-2464 or execdir@mainebarexaminers.org for assistance. \nPromulgation Date: 8/3/2026 FOR THE COURT: \n \n \n   /s/      \nVALERIE STANFILL \nChief Justice \n \nAndrew M. Mead \nCatherine R. Connors \nRick E. Lawrence \nWayne R. Douglas \nJulia M. Lipez \nChristopher C. Taub",
      "title": "Standing Order: Standing Order on Servicemembers or Spouses of Servicemembers Seeking Admission to the Maine Bar"
    },
